<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Anbeeco half yr shr, div falls.</title>
<headline>Anbeeco half yr shr, div falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Oct 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   7.4	   vs 12.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 2.5	   vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Headline earnings     1.11	  vs 1.89</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.78	  vs 3.52</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.67	  vs 1.31</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.61	  vs 0.30</p>
<p>    Turnover		  38.23	 vs 38.88</p>
<p>Div payable Feb 14</p>
<p>on register Jan 31</p>
<p>Full name: Anbeeco Investment Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said retail markets were unlikely to show a significant improvement in the next six months. However, the group would continue to trade aggressively and was well positioned to benefit from an upturn in conditions.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
